From: Felipe Infante de Castro <18445184+fidecastro@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:42:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] platform/surface: aggregator_registry: Add the RTC on the
 Surface Laptop 7

The Surface Laptop 7 keeps its time in SAM, as the Surface Laptop 8
does. On a 15-inch model (microsoft,romulus15) SAM answers the requests
rtc-surface uses: a "get Unix time" request (target category 0x01,
command 0x10) through the cdev interface returned the time, 2 seconds
behind an NTP-synchronised system clock.

With the RTC device in the Laptop 7's group, rtc-surface binds
("surface_rtc 01:01:01:00:00: registered as rtc1"), reads that time, and
a hwclock --systohc on it is accepted and read back within a second.

The group is also used by the 13.8-inch model (microsoft,romulus13),
which has the same firmware family but was not tested.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.2
Signed-off-by: Felipe Infante de Castro <18445184+fidecastro@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
index a7c1d52..fb5036c 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
@@ -312,6 +312,7 @@ static const struct software_node *ssam_node_group_sl6[] = {
 /* Devices for Surface Laptop 7. */
 static const struct software_node *ssam_node_group_sl7[] = {
 	&ssam_node_root,
+	&ssam_node_sam_rtc,
 	&ssam_node_tmp_perf_profile_with_fan,
 	&ssam_node_fan_speed,
 	&ssam_node_hid_sam_keyboard,
